    "body": "> I would like to understand this better.\r\n> \r\n> 1. If both preload and actual have integrity metadata that matches, there's no problem.\r\n> 2. If both preload and actual have integrity metadata and it doesn't match, the consumed response ends up rejected later due to the integrity metadata check on actual.\r\n> 3. If preload has integrity metadata and actual does not, there's no problem.\r\n> 4. If preload does not have integrity metadata and actual does, the consumed response ends up rejected later due to the integrity metadata check on actual.\r\n> \r\n> Note that until [whatwg/fetch@92b3578](https://github.com/whatwg/fetch/commit/92b35785b2b70cd4f7cfa70e02f8bc03ef133eb1) landed 2 and 4 were problematic, but I think they no longer are.\r\n> \r\n> Am I missing anything? Do we have tests for these scenarios?\r\n\r\nAnd 5: preload and actual both have different but matching integrity metadata, e.g. with a different sha algorithm.\r\n\r\nThis is quite well tested: https://wpt.live/preload/subresource-integrity.html\r\n",
